# Alias AI Privacy Airgap Rules

When generating code, analyzing codebase files, or suggesting shell commands:
1. Preserve all `<ALIAS_*>` placeholders (e.g. `<ALIAS_VIN_1>`, `<ALIAS_IBAN_1>`, `<ALIAS_APIKEY_1>`). Do not replace them with dummy values.
2. Route any LLM client or agent requests through the local Alias AI transparent gateway at `http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1`.
3. Never write plaintext credentials (API keys, DB connection strings, AWS tokens) into git commits, documentation, or public scratchpads.
4. Verify that the local Alias AI gateway is running (`npx alias-ai start`) for zero-knowledge cloud egress.

